# Scheduled Task Detection — Test Cases

## Purpose

This test suite validates the detection logic for suspicious scheduled-task executable paths and execution arguments.

It uses synthetic test data to validate detection behavior independently of the production Sentinel telemetry.

**MITRE ATT&CK:** T1053.005 — Scheduled Task/Job: Scheduled Task

## Test Coverage

| Test Case | Scenario | Expected Result |
|---|---|---|
| TC01 | Executable in `C:\Users\Public\` | Match |
| TC02 | PowerShell with `-EncodedCommand` | Match |
| TC03 | Legitimate executable with normal arguments | No match |
| TC04 | Risky path with hidden execution | Match |
| TC05 | Legitimate monitoring executable | No match |
| TC06 | Executable in `AppData\Roaming` | Match |

## KQL Test Harness

```kql
let TestData = datatable(
    TestCase:string,
    ExecutablePath:string,
    Arguments:string,
    ExpectedMatch:bool
)
[
    "TC01",
    @"C:\Users\Public\update.exe",
    "Normal",
    true,

    "TC02",
    @"C:\Windows\System32\powershell.exe",
    "-EncodedCommand ABC123",
    true,

    "TC03",
    @"C:\Program Files\Backup\agent.exe",
    "Normal",
    false,

    "TC04",
    @"C:\Users\Public\update.exe",
    "-WindowStyle Hidden",
    true,

    "TC05",
    @"C:\Program Files\Monitoring\agent.exe",
    "Normal",
    false,

    "TC06",
    @"C:\Users\john\AppData\Roaming\update.exe",
    "Normal",
    true
];

TestData
| extend NormalizedPath = tolower(ExecutablePath)
| extend NormalizedArguments = tolower(Arguments)

| extend SuspiciousPath =
    NormalizedPath contains @"\users\public\"
    or NormalizedPath contains @"\appdata\roaming\"
    or NormalizedPath contains @"\appdata\local\temp\"
    or NormalizedPath contains @"\windows\temp\"

| extend EncodedPowerShell =
    NormalizedArguments matches regex
    @"(?i)(?:^|\s)-(?:encodedcommand|enc|ec)(?:\s|=|:)"

| extend HiddenExecution =
    NormalizedArguments matches regex
    @"(?i)-windowstyle\s+hidden"

| extend ExecutionPolicyBypass =
    NormalizedArguments matches regex
    @"(?i)-executionpolicy\s+bypass"

| extend SuspiciousArguments =
    EncodedPowerShell
    or HiddenExecution
    or ExecutionPolicyBypass

| extend ActualMatch =
    SuspiciousPath or SuspiciousArguments

| extend TestResult = iff(
    ActualMatch == ExpectedMatch,
    "PASS",
    "FAIL"
)

| extend DetectionReason = case(
    SuspiciousPath and SuspiciousArguments,
        "Risky path + suspicious arguments",
    SuspiciousPath,
        "Risky executable path",
    SuspiciousArguments,
        "Suspicious execution arguments",
    "No suspicious indicators"
)

| project
    TestCase,
    ExecutablePath,
    Arguments,
    SuspiciousPath,
    SuspiciousArguments,
    DetectionReason,
    ExpectedMatch,
    ActualMatch,
    TestResult

| order by TestCase asc
```

## Expected Results

All six test cases should return `PASS`.

| Test Case | Expected Detection |
|---|---|
| TC01 | Suspicious executable path |
| TC02 | Suspicious execution arguments |
| TC03 | No detection |
| TC04 | Risky path + suspicious arguments |
| TC05 | No detection |
| TC06 | Suspicious executable path |

## Validation Notes

- These tests validate the synthetic detection logic.
- They do not prove that production Windows event fields are extracted correctly.
- They do not establish that every attacker technique or argument variation is covered.
- Additional tests should be added as new false positives and detection gaps are discovered.

## Future Test Improvements

1. Add variations in PowerShell argument casing and spacing.
2. Test quoted executable paths.
3. Test additional PowerShell encoded-command abbreviations.
4. Add legitimate software scenarios involving user-writable directories.
5. Add tests using sanitized real Windows event payloads.
6. Validate task creation and modification events independently.

## Current Status

- Six synthetic test cases: previously validated.
- Production event extraction: pending final schema validation.
- Real-world false-positive coverage: ongoing.
